        <h1>You don’t need another to-do list. You need someone to do the list.</h1>
        <p>Starting is the hardest part—so don’t be the one who starts. AI for ADHD builds you a personalized AI task-completion system where dedicated digital Allies break down the chaos, draft the work, and prep the finish line. You just approve and move on.</p>

        <h2>Meet Your Personal AI Crew: Digital Allies Who Have Your Back</h2>
        <ul>
            <li><strong>The Sorter:</strong> Kills the "Everything is Urgent" Tornado. Acts as the bouncer for your attention—scanning brain-dumps, notes, and inbox chaos, stripping out the noise, and handing you a clean, realistic game plan.</li>
            <li><strong>The Breaker:</strong> Kills the "Too Big to Start" Wall. Slices massive, vague, overwhelming projects into tiny, frictionless micro-steps—handing you only Step 1 while prepping the rest in the background.</li>
            <li><strong>The Chaser:</strong> Kills the Boring Admin Quicksand. Goes down the rabbit holes for you—summarizing long docs, comparing options, and gathering context so you make decisions in 30 seconds instead of opening 15 browser tabs.</li>
            <li><strong>The Starter:</strong> Kills Blank-Page Dread. Takes care of the dreadful first 80%—drafting the awkward emails you've been avoiding, outlining the project, and writing the ugly first drafts—so you just approve and hit send.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>How the Crew Relay Works</h2>
        <p>Your Allies work like a relay team. They catch the chaos, chop it down, grab the info, and draft the work—so you just step in at the 90-yard line and walk it into the end zone. Delegation over discipline: stop trying harder and start having the work taken off your hands.</p>

